    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "The hq binary is the first client of the ledger and, by thesis §5, runs the same ledger implementation the server will. This spec founds hqgit-cli: a clap frame whose subcommands are one module each, exit codes mapped in exactly one place through Error::exit_code, a --json mode on every read verb that emits canonical sorted-key JSON, layered configuration (user and repository), and the three verbs that prove the local repository works: hq init creates .hq/ with a local ed25519 identity and the genesis entry, hq status reports heads and identity, and hq log renders entries in total order. Later specs add verbs by extending main.rs and cli.rs; nothing here talks to a network or to git.\n",
    "title": "The hq binary: clap frame, exit codes, JSON output, init, status, log"
  },
